WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.468 --> 00:00:02.901
[music]

2
00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:08.838
[Instructor] Alright so it's time
to get started working on Prototype 4.

3
00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:12.270
Make sure to download
the starter Project files

4
00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.700
in the link below
the video, and since

5
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.630
we've already done this
a couple of times,

6
00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.765
I'll just open up my Project
inside of Unity.

7
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.347
Open up your Scenes Folder
in the Project window.

8
00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:25.008
Open up your Prototype 4.

9
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.053
Delete your "SampleScene".

10
00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:34.115
Now we have our next
Prototype set up.

11
00:00:36.365 --> 00:00:38.430
Now you can see down
in the bottom here

12
00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:42.799
we actually have a different
perspective on our Camera.

13
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.020
So if I select our Camera,

14
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.840
our "Projection" is currently
set to "Orthographic",

15
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.852
so it has a lot more
of a...

16
00:00:50.512 --> 00:00:54.761
flatter look to it versus 
that "Perspective View" that we have.

17
00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:58.870
If you want your "Scene View"
to be the same

18
00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:01.180
as your "Game View",
you can actually select

19
00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:03.584
underneath the different
coordinates on the top-right

20
00:01:03.584 --> 00:01:06.445
of the Scene view instead
of the Perspective View

21
00:01:06.445 --> 00:01:10.550
which has this triangular cone shape
next to it.

22
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:13.149
We can select the "Isometric View",

23
00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:17.219
which then gives us the 3 bars,

24
00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.255
kind of a square shape.
And we can now see

25
00:01:20.255 --> 00:01:22.255
our game just like it looks

26
00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.110
in our Game View.

27
00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.700
For now I'm going to just
keep it as perspective,

28
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.703
so it's easier to see,

29
00:01:32.426 --> 00:01:34.436
where I place things for now.

30
00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:38.151
And then in fact, you can run
the game right now.

31
00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.100
So if you press the Play button,
you'll see all

32
00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.930
of these cool Particle Effects
drifting in the Background

33
00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:48.940
kind of like clouds in the sky.

34
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.773
Now we're ready to get started.
Alright.

35
00:01:53.773 --> 00:01:56.420
So what you're going to do is open
up Unity Hub,

36
00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:00.192
and create a Prototype 4
Project in your Course Directory.

37
00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.580
Make sure to head to the link
below this video

38
00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:04.660
to download the Project starter files,

39
00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.166
and import them into your new
Unity Project.

40
00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.038
Open up the Prototype 4 Scene,
and delete

41
00:02:10.038 --> 00:02:11.970
the SampleScene without saving,

42
00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.050
and then if you want to test
that you can click "Run"

43
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:16.133
to see the Particle Effects 
in our Project.

44
00:02:16.327 --> 00:02:18.327
So now it's your turn.

45
00:02:20.041 --> 00:02:21.925
[music]
